### Job Scheduler API — requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension
### Click "Send Request" above any line below to run it.
### App must be running on localhost:8080 first.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/jobs

### 1. Submit a reliable job (ECHO)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ECHO",
  "payload": "hello world",
  "priority": 3,
  "maxAttempts": 3
}

### 2. Submit a flaky job (watch retries / dead-lettering)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FLAKY",
  "payload": "test-1",
  "priority": 5,
  "maxAttempts": 4
}

### 3. Submit a high-priority job (jumps the queue ahead of lower priority)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ECHO",
  "payload": "urgent job",
  "priority": 1,
  "maxAttempts": 1
}

### 4. Get a single job by id — replace {id} with a real id from a response above
GET {{baseUrl}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 5. List all jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 6. List only jobs with a specific status
GET {{baseUrl}}?status=SUCCESS

###
GET {{baseUrl}}?status=RETRYING

###
GET {{baseUrl}}?status=DEAD_LETTER

### 7. Cancel a job — only works while it's still PENDING
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 8. Submit with an unknown type — should return 400, not a silent failure
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "NOT_A_REAL_TYPE",
  "payload": "should fail validation"
}
